<chapter xml:id="ch-algebra-calculus">
  <title>Algebra and Calculus</title>
  
  <introduction>
  <p>
    In the previous chapter, we introduced the basics of symbolic computation.
    We can create symbolic variables and perform basic operations on them.
    In this chapter, we will see how to use symbolic computation to perform algebraic manipulations and calculus operations.
  </p>
  <p>
    Also, the following are needed to run the code in this chapter:</p>
    <program language="julia">
      <code>
        using Symbolics, Latexify
        @variables x 
      </code>
    </program>
  
  </introduction>

  <section xml:id="sect-equations">
    <title>Equations</title>
    <p>
      Equations are created with with a <c>~</c>, because the <c>=</c> is used for variable assignment.  For example, the equation <m>x^2 - 4x = 5</m> is created with 
    </p>
    <program language="julia">
      <code>
        eq = x^2 - 4x ~ 5
      </code>
    </program>
    <p>And the output is <m>- 4 \cdot x + x^{2} = 5</m> </p>
    <p>We will see how to solve this below, but a few items to notice.  First, the output of the left side was rearranged.  This is common </p>
  </section>
</chapter>